# build outputs
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
# The blank RAM image is a source input, not a build product: it is a fixed
# one-word image meaning "memory starts empty", and the UART-loader checks, the
# FPGA flow, and axhost all reference it by path with nothing generating it.
# Keep the exception adjacent to the broad rule that would otherwise hide it.
!sw/bootrom/blank.hex
*.map
obj_dir*/
build/
# isolated FPGA synth trees from `make -C rtl/fpga ... BUILD=build-<tag>`
build-*/

# aXsim binary
sim/axsim/axsim

# simulation artifacts
*.vcd
*.fst
*.fst.hier
trace.log
__pycache__/

# FPGA flow outputs
*.json
# Component manifests and supplied build profiles are source inputs, not
# generated FPGA JSON. Keep these exceptions adjacent to the broad rule so
# new profiles are visible to Git by default.
!components/**/component.json
!configs/*.json
# Everything under research/ is a checked contract, record or measurement --
# never synthesis output. Naming subdirectories individually meant that
# research/personalities, research/comparisons and research/partial-reconfig
# were silently ignored and never committed, so CI failed on a fresh checkout
# with "no JSON contract documents found" while the files sat on the author's
# disk. Cover the whole tree so a new research subdirectory cannot repeat it.
!research/**/*.json
# Verification manifests are source inputs, not generated tool output.
!tests/verification-suites.json
*.asc
*.bit
*.svf
# Generated FPGA artifacts never belong in Git. Release identity is recorded
# as hashes in the hardware achievement documentation instead.

# Browser bundle. The page sources in sim/web/public/ are tracked; the compiled
# machine and the payload staged beside them are build products of
# `make -C sim/web build` (payload.hex is already covered by *.hex above).
sim/web/public/axsoc.js
sim/web/public/axsoc.wasm
sim/web/public/.bundle-tag
# The side-by-side page's staged bundles: one compiled machine per selection,
# plus the manifest and the core manifests the page reads. All generated by
# `make -C sim/web machines`; the page sources beside them stay tracked.
sim/web/public/machines/

# editor noise
*.swp
.vscode/
# Formal-generated jobs, solver databases, and counterexample traces.
formal/build/
sim/unit/morph_outputs.bin

# libFuzzer working directory: the generated corpus, the built harness, and any
# crash artifact. A crash worth keeping is promoted to sim/fuzz/corpus/ by hand.
sim/fuzz/build/
sim/fuzz/crash-*
sim/fuzz/leak-*
sim/fuzz/timeout-*
sim/fuzz/oom-*
# ...but a promoted seed is source, not output. Without this the global *.elf
# rule above silently drops the regression corpus, and a checked-in seed that
# was never checked in is worse than none: the claim outlives the file.
!sim/fuzz/corpus/*.elf
